{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7EXRg12wfwBnYP1B73Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I write, a few questions. Each answer would change what the page says:\n\n1. **Who is the page for?** Owners with W-2 stylists on commission, owners who rent booths, or both? Their money problems are different (tips and commission payroll on one side, rent collection and 1099s on the other), and I'd write the opening to match.\n2. **What usually makes a salon owner call you?** For example: a sales tax notice, payroll on a Sunday night, a shoebox of receipts in March. If you have a line a client actually said to you, that's even better.\n3. **Which booking or POS systems do you work with?** Square, Vagaro, Boulevard, GlossGenius? Naming them shows you know salons in a way \"monthly books\" doesn't.\n4. **Should the page mention the 3 missed close dates and the price increase from $149?** I'd suggest stating the 10th as your normal close date without promising it as a guarantee, and showing $199 without the history. But if you'd rather be upfront about either one, I can write it that way.\n5. **What name should I use, and what should the button say?** Your name or business name, plus button text if you have something in mind. Otherwise I'll use \"Book your free 20-minute call.\"\n\nIf you don't know something, just say so and I'll leave it out instead of guessing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_read_input_tokens":9515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":375},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ff30114-1751-4d0f-8904-176bb09c0d5b","uuid":"cba43668-96d0-4265-a845-432ce4a842cc","timestam